{"schemaVersion":1,"reviewId":"canonical-chemistry-q1-soaps","ruleVersion":"semantic-atomicity-v1","landscapeId":"c436b994-8f44-5134-b9f8-0c9f5d6a5ba0","goalId":"6765f741-42a6-55c5-a218-81b883b1f5ae","fingerprint":"sha256:0f310f33585727344241cd12f60c0a8402b1b09abbbcbd79e6c78601bb2f2583","status":"atomic","semanticAtomic":true,"reviewedAt":"2026-10-05","reviewer":"Codex independent seven current A/M scientific review","reason":"A single practical preparation chain includes actual alkaline fat hydrolysis, product explanation and salting-out separation of the soap. Glycerol and fatty-acid salts are correct, and salting out does not itself cleave the fat. Actual practical execution remains assessable and cannot be inferred from an image or supplied log.","suggestedSplit":[]}
{"schemaVersion":1,"reviewId":"canonical-chemistry-q1-soaps","ruleVersion":"semantic-atomicity-v1","landscapeId":"c436b994-8f44-5134-b9f8-0c9f5d6a5ba0","goalId":"6966df95-f125-5ecc-af8e-0442545d9f17","fingerprint":"sha256:540249b7a5e5e2fc0e171c330ef2c93fefc0136d4a8f3a5153e68abc0776f017","status":"atomic","semanticAtomic":true,"reviewedAt":"2026-10-05","reviewer":"Codex independent seven current A/M scientific review","reason":"One amphiphilic structure-to-arrangement model explains interfaces, micelles, emulsification and surface-tension reduction. An oil droplet is distinguished from a micelle; unrelated quantitative soap-pH measurement is not absorbed into this goal.","suggestedSplit":[]}
